-- Spec EMIT-5: a command the nexus evaluates itself, with no language
-- pool, holds chains of `&&`, `||` and guards of any length: the manifest
-- nests no deeper for a longer chain. An operand after the one that
-- decides a chain does not run, nor does an arm whose test fails. A let
-- before every element of a chain, or a long run of lets, nests no deeper
-- either. A let before an element is seen by every later element and
-- shadows what it names, and is evaluated only when the chain reaches it.
module main (allOf, anyOf, pick, stopAnd, stopOr, pickThrow, classify, letGuards, letRun, letChain, scopeA, lazyLet)

